# The Endstone: "you play a land or cast a spell" is its controller's alone (CR 603.2): Bot2 playing a land and casting spells
# draws Bot1 nothing. Its end-step clause sets the life total, it doesn't only lower it (CR 119.5): after Bot2's Lightning Bolt
# takes Bot1 from 10 to 7, Bot1's next end step makes it 10 again, a gain of 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
The Endstone
Forest
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Endstone.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 10
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 7
? Bot1.Hand = Forest
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 10
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island
